# Batch Wave 1 — Hub/Runner Split Foundations

## Context

Architecture decided (task artifact `runner-architecture.md` v10): split sidecar into **hub** (`@slayzone/hub`, owns DB/routers/auth/fan-out) + N **runners** (`@slayzone/runner`, exec: pty/agents/git/processes/fs) dialing out over one authed wss. Wave 1 = the 13 independently-mergeable foundation units: 7 behavior-preserving DB-decoupling refactors (exec code stops touching DB directly, goes behind injected ops interfaces) + 6 dark greenfield units (protocol, auth, schema, CLI plumbing, REST surface, TLS identity). Integration wave later.

## Delivery model — NO PRs, NO pushed branches (waves 1-3 autonomous, user-authorized 2026-07-10)

- Each worker runs in an **isolated git worktree** (harness-managed), implements its unit, verifies, **does NOT commit, push, or create PRs**. Worker exports its change as a binary patch (excluding pnpm-lock.yaml) to the session scratchpad + reports verification results.
- Orchestrator applies patches to the main working tree unit-by-unit (path-disjoint by design), re-verifies, then **commits locally to main (never pushes)** — required so wave N+1 worktrees fork from a base containing wave N. Per-unit commits stage only patch-owned paths (pre-existing dirty files in the main tree are never swept in).
- Lockfile: orchestrator re-runs `pnpm install` after applying package.json changes; workers never ship lockfile hunks.

## Cutover strategy (wave 3 tail)

Strangler flip: `fleet_mode: legacy | runner` boot setting. `legacy` = in-process exec (today, byte-identical); `runner` = composition wires runner-proxy impls over the fleet gateway to the auto-spawned local runner. Flip at boot only (live ptys can't migrate processes); rollback = flip back. Legacy path deleted in wave 4, not before.

## Verification recipe (per worker, in its worktree)

1. `pnpm install`
2. `pnpm typecheck`
3. Affected-package vitest (e.g. `pnpm --filter @slayzone/terminal test` / dir-local vitest)
4. **Prod build** (`pnpm build`) — typecheck alone hides module-resolution bugs in this repo
5. **Refactor units (1–7) only:** scoped e2e after build — run terminal/task Playwright specs (`pnpm test:e2e -- <spec>`), with `env -u ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` (leaked var poisons e2e in dogfood terminals). Greenfield units (8–13) are dark (no runtime surface): unit tests + build suffice.

