## Cross-unit rules (every worker prompt)

- Barrel imports only between packages; never deep paths.
- Do NOT touch: `packages/apps/server/src/composition.ts`, `packages/apps/app/src/main/index.ts`, `packages/shared/transport/src/server/app-deps.ts`, `router.ts`; `migrations.ts` reserved for unit 10 only; `rest-api/index.ts` reserved for unit 12 only.
- Zero behavior change (refactor units: same SQL, same ordering/async semantics; greenfield: dark).
- Theme tokens / lint rules apply (`pnpm lint`).
- NO commit, NO push, NO PR — leave the worktree dirty; report a summary + verification results + `git diff --stat`.

## Worker instructions template (appended verbatim to each prompt)

```
After implementing:
1. Invoke Skill tool skill:"code-review" — fix findings it surfaces.
2. pnpm typecheck; run the affected package's vitest suite.
3. pnpm build (prod build must pass).
4. [refactor units only] Run scoped e2e: build outputs, then the terminal/task Playwright specs, with env -u ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE.
5. DO NOT commit, push, or create any PR/branch. Leave changes uncommitted in the worktree.
6. Final message: what changed, verification results (each step pass/fail with output tail on failure), `git diff --stat`, and any deviations from spec.
```

## Tracking

Status table maintained as workers report; per-unit diff applied to main tree after verification review; final combined typecheck+build+e2e on main tree; commits only after user approval.

